markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>What Is a Flowchart, and Why AI Needs to Read It</h1>

<p>That wraps up functions. The next lesson shifts to a different question: not just what code does when it runs, but how it decides what to do in the first place. Let's start with flowcharts.</p>

<p>Think about a social media app deciding what to show you after you like one video. Someone designed that rule. Apps are full of <b>decision points</b> like this, and each one shapes what a user sees or experiences next. Before students write a single conditional in code, this lesson asks them to notice that decisions like this exist everywhere, and that someone, eventually maybe them, is the one designing the rule.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Flowchart</b> is a diagram that shows the steps in a process using shapes and arrows. Flowcharts make it easier to plan and visualize how a program or process works.</p>
</div>

---

<h2 style="color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:6px;">The Four Symbols</h2>

<p style="margin-top:0;">Flowcharts use a small, standardized set of shapes. Each shape has a specific job:</p>

<div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:32px; width:100%; box-sizing:border-box; margin:24px 0;">

 <!-- HTML Flowchart -->
 <div style="flex:0 1 300px; display:flex; justify-content:center;">

  <div aria-hidden="true" style="position:relative; width:280px; height:240px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border:1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius:12px; box-shadow:0 2px 7px rgba(0,0,0,0.10);">

   <!-- Connectors behind the shapes -->

 <!-- Top vertical connector -->
  <div style="position:absolute; left:138px; top:40px; width:4px; height:28px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <!-- Process to decision -->
   <div style="position:absolute; left:138px; top:98px; width:4px; height:38px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <!-- Left branch -->
   <div style="position:absolute; left:38px; top:80px; width:60px; height:4px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <div style="position:absolute; left:38px; top:80px; width:4px; height:70px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <div style="position:absolute; left:38px; top:146px; width:70px; height:4px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>
   
   <!-- Decision to bottom -->
   <div style="position:absolute; left:138px; top:170px; width:4px; height:35px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <!-- Right branch -->
  <div style="position:absolute; left:172px; top:146px; width:66px; height:4px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <div style="position:absolute; left:234px; top:146px; width:4px; height:68px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

 <div style="position:absolute; left:180px; top:210px; width:58px; height:4px; background-color:#0093A4; z-index:1;"></div>

   <!-- Start oval -->
  <div style="position:absolute; left:95px; top:10px; width:90px; height:32px; background-color:#E4E2F8; border:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:20px; box-sizing:border-box; z-index:2;"></div>

   <!-- Process rectangle -->
   <div style="position:absolute; left:95px; top:62px; width:90px; height:40px; background-color:#D5EFFF; border:4px solid #176B87; border-radius:3px; box-sizing:border-box; z-index:2;"></div>

   <!-- Decision diamond -->
  <div style="position:absolute; left:114px; top:124px; width:52px; height:52px; background-color:#FFE4C2; border:4px solid #A44F00; box-sizing:border-box; transform:rotate(45deg); z-index:2;"></div>

   <!-- End oval -->
   <div style="position:absolute; left:95px; top:198px; width:90px; height:32px; background-color:#E4E2F8; border:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:20px; box-sizing:border-box; z-index:2;"></div>

  </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Color-coded vocabulary -->
  <div style="flex:1 1 420px; min-width:0;">

<!-- Start/End -->
  <div style="margin-bottom:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <span style="display:inline-block; background-color:#E4E2F8; color:#1F1976; border:2px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:18px; padding:4px 10px; margin-right:6px; font-weight:bold;">
        Start/End · Oval
      </span>
      where the process begins or stops
    </div>

<!-- Process -->
<div style="margin-bottom:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <span style="display:inline-block; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#06338D; border:2px solid #176B87; border-radius:5px; padding:4px 10px; margin-right:6px; font-weight:bold;">
        Process · Rectangle
      </span>
      an action the app or user takes
    </div>

<!-- Decision -->
  <div style="margin-bottom:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <span style="display:inline-block; background-color:#FFE4C2; color:#713600; border:2px solid #A44F00; border-radius:5px; padding:4px 10px; margin-right:6px; font-weight:bold;">
        Decision · Diamond
      </span>
      a question with Yes/No outcomes
    </div>

 <!-- Connector -->
<div style="line-height:1.5;">
      <span style="display:inline-block; background-color:#D7F3F5; color:#005E68; border:2px solid #0093A4; border-radius:18px; padding:4px 10px; margin-right:6px; font-weight:bold;">
        Connector · Line
      </span>
      shows the flow of logic from one step to the next
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

---


<h2 style="color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:8px;">A Flowchart in Action</h2>

<p>Knowing the symbols is the first step. Next, look at how they work together to show a complete process.</p>

<p>Consider a weather app deciding which message to show. It checks whether the temperature is greater than 70. The answer determines which message appears on the page.</p>

<div role="group" aria-label="Flowchart showing how a weather app chooses a message based on whether the temperature is greater than 70" style="max-width:650px; margin:24px auto; padding:24px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border:1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius:12px; box-shadow:0 2px 7px rgba(0,0,0,0.10); box-sizing:border-box; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

  <!-- Start -->
  <div style="width:190px; min-height:52px; margin:0 auto; padding:10px 16px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#E4E2F8; color:#1F1976; border:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:30px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold;">
    Check the temperature
  </div>

  <!-- Connector -->
  <div aria-hidden="true" style="width:4px; height:30px; margin:0 auto; background-color:#0093A4;"></div>

  <!-- Decision -->
  <div style="width:112px; height:112px; margin:0 auto; background-color:#FFE4C2; border:4px solid #A44F00; box-sizing:border-box; transform:rotate(45deg); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
    <div style="width:96px; text-align:center; color:#713600; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.2; transform:rotate(-45deg);">
      Is the<br>temperature<br>&gt; 70?
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Connector from decision -->
  <div aria-hidden="true" style="width:4px; height:30px; margin:0 auto; background-color:#0093A4;"></div>

  <!-- Split connector -->
  <div aria-hidden="true" style="position:relative; width:60%; height:36px; margin:0 auto; border-top:4px solid #0093A4; border-left:4px solid #0093A4; border-right:4px solid #0093A4; box-sizing:border-box;">

  <span style="position:absolute; left:8px; top:5px; background-color:#D7F3F5; color:#005E68; border-radius:12px; padding:2px 8px; font-size:14px; font-weight:bold;">
      Yes
    </span>

  <span style="position:absolute; right:8px; top:5px; background-color:#D7F3F5; color:#005E68; border-radius:12px; padding:2px 8px; font-size:14px; font-weight:bold;">
      No
    </span>

  </div>

  <!-- Outcomes -->
  <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:stretch; width:100%; gap:20%;">

  <div style="width:40%; min-height:90px; padding:12px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#06338D; border:4px solid #176B87; border-radius:5px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.35;">
      Show:<br>
      “It’s warm outside!”
    </div>

  <div style="width:40%; min-height:90px; padding:12px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#06338D; border:4px solid #176B87; border-radius:5px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.35;">
      Show:<br>
      “It’s cool outside!”
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Merge connector -->
  <div aria-hidden="true" style="width:60%; height:36px; margin:0 auto; border-bottom:4px solid #0093A4; border-left:4px solid #0093A4; border-right:4px solid #0093A4; box-sizing:border-box;"></div>

  <div aria-hidden="true" style="width:4px; height:30px; margin:0 auto; background-color:#0093A4;"></div>

  <!-- End -->
  <div style="width:190px; min-height:52px; margin:0 auto; padding:10px 16px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#E4E2F8; color:#1F1976; border:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:30px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold;">
    Message appears
  </div>

</div>

<p>Follow the connectors from top to bottom. The diamond checks whether <code>temperature &gt; 70</code>. A Yes or No answer leads to a different message, but both paths complete the same process.</p>

---

<h2>Why AI Needs to Read It Too</h2>

<p>When a flowchart is shared as an image, AI can use computer vision to recognize its shapes, read its text, and translate the visual plan into working code.</p>


<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p><strong>💡 Teacher tip:</strong> standardization matters here for two audiences at once. It's what makes a student's flowchart readable by a classmate or by you. But it's also what makes AI able to correctly interpret a photo of that flowchart and build a working program from it. A messy, non-standard flowchart isn't just harder for people to follow, it's harder for AI to translate accurately too.</p>
</div>

<p>Next, you'll see how one specific shape, the decision diamond, becomes a specific piece of code: the conditional statement.</p>


MARKDOWN
